    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0641" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1948v03/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/2–448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-02-04T19:00:00+00:00">February 4, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>429. While discussing a number of questions with Sargent<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d389-f1"/> today I said to him that any developments at this
                    juncture threatening stability of French Government would give US concern. Sir
                    Orme said that Foreign Office would view such developments similarly. In fact,
                    when franc devaluation discussions were going on every directive to negotiators
                    had been accompanied with caveat that matters were not to be pressed to point
                    where Schuman Government would be overthrown. Foreign Office, he added, adhered
                    to view that any weakening of Schuman Government at this time would be very
                    serious development.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 429; repeated Paris 35.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="1" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>Sir Orme G. Sargent, British Permanent Under-Secretary of State for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
